WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:05.660
HBO has just put out a second Game of Thrones
Season 6 trailer, and some short clips from

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.819
the first few episodes.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:09.950
There’s some crazy new stuff here, so let’s
have a quick look.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.170
Again, the trailer starts at the Wall, with
the body of Jon Snow.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:18.189
Davos and Ghost and some loyal Night’s Watchmen
seem to be defending Jon’s body from the

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:23.140
Watchmen who killed him – including Alliser
Thorne, Bowen Marsh, and everyone’s favourite

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.550
black brother, Olly.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:28.199
Melisandre’s around as well, so again this
will probably eventually somehow lead to the

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:30.009
resurrection of Jon.

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:35.580
Whether this’ll involve sacrifice or fire
or blood or Ghost or white walkers we don’t

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.890
yet know for sure.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:41.530
We also see more of Bastardbowl, the big battle
fought between the Boltons and the wildlings

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:43.800
and the north just outside Winterfell.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.140
You can see the heraldry of Houses Hornwood
and Mormont, and the Umbers with the Boltons,

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.880
and Davos is here, beneath a Stark banner.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.410
We also see Tormund, and Ramsay, and the big
friendly giant Wun Wun bursting through what

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:00.410
looks to be the gates of Winterfell, and also
that horse leading the cavalry charge might

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.410
be Jon’s.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.760
There’s a clip of Theon and Sansa running
through the snow to escape the Boltons, and

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.210
we later see Sansa at the battlefield wearing
Stark clothes.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:13.020
She talks about the people who took from her,
over shots of Ramsay, and of what looks to

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:17.540
be a Frey wedding, with Lord Walder and Lannister
soldiers.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:23.630
This could be where Sansa and the Starks take
revenge, a Red Wedding 2.0, where Freys and

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:27.320
Lannisters are slaughtered to avenge Robb
and Cat and Ned.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.360
This could involve the Blackfish, the brotherhood
without banners, maybe Arya if she crosses

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.560
the narrow sea…

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.570
We don’t really know how it’ll go down
but one way or another the Freys will finally

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.560
get what’s coming to em.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.500
In Braavos, Arya’s still in the House of
Black and White with the Faceless Men, still

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.950
blind, though she seems to get her sight back
at some point – here she’s sparring, getting

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:51.690
slapped up by the Waif, and then she’s told
she’s on her second and last chance by Jaqen

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:58.010
H’ghar, or rather, by someone who’s wearing
Jaqen’s face – remember, last season,

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.830
someone with Jaqen’s face took poison and
died.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:06.280
So, remember that any Faceless Man can wear
any face, they don’t really have personal

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:11.810
identities, they are no one – which is what
they’re trying to make Arya.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.830
But it doesn’t look like Arya is willing
to let go of who she is.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:22.230
Further east, in Meereen, Tyrion, Varys, Missandei
and Grey Worm try to hold things together.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:26.840
It looks like they’re challenged by the
Great Masters, the original rulers of Meereen,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:30.920
and the Sons of the Harpy are still a threat,
and we meet a new player, apparently called

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.450
Kinvara – a red priestess like Melisandre.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.700
She’s looking pretty pleased with herself
here so it’ll be really cool to see what

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.530
this new red woman brings to the table.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:45.130
We also see Tyrion talking about dragons not
liking captivity, and then he sees Rhaegal

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.520
and Viserion for himself in the Great Pyramid
basement.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.870
So we can probably expect the dragons to finally
be let loose sometime soon.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:57.990
We see Daenerys in Vaes Dothrak, the sacred
city of the Dothraki.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:03.100
She’s stripped and downtrodden – has her
power and prestige taken away from her.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:08.370
These women are probably the dosh khaleen,
the ex-wives of khals who in Dothraki culture

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.819
are expected to live in Vaes Dothrak.

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:14.959
Jorah’s coming to try to and save her, and
he’s bringing his deadly greyscale with

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:20.170
him, but Dany’s salvation will probably
be Drogon, so Dany can answer the disrespect

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:23.660
of the Dothraki with fire and blood.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:28.460
On the Iron Islands we get a bit of a Greyjoy
family reunion – Theon meets with Asha – or

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:32.330
Yara – and uncle Euron turns up to kill
his brother Balon.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:36.500
And it’s starting to look like Asha is taking
on the role of Victarion from the books, meaning

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.910
after the kingsmoot, she may be sailing east,
to Meereen to meet Daenerys – the evidence

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:46.520
is that this girl Asha is making out with
looks like a slave from Volantis – and the

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.760
only reason Asha’d be in Volantis would
be as a pit stop to Meereen.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:54.160
So maybe Asha will meet the dragon queen.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.440
In King’s Landing, Cersei Lannister is mad
as hell.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:02.349
Jaime has brought back the body of Myrcella,
leaving Tommen her only surviving child, and

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:05.580
the sparrows still have Margaery and Loras
Tyrell.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:10.530
Cersei sends Jaime up against the High Sparrow,
and shit gets real quick – a Tyrell army

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:15.220
approaches the Great Sept, and Lord Mace wears
a funny hat, Robert Strong is let loose on

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.959
the sparrows, and there is blood.

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:21.720
At some point it looks like Jaime goes to
the riverlands, which is something that happens

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.720
in the books.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.949
Brienne and Podrick also seem to be there,
and Pod is jumped by Bronn.

00:04:26.949 --> 00:04:31.270
With Jaime, Brienne and Pod all in the riverlands,
it might be that they take part in the Stark

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:36.729
vengeance at the Frey wedding, they might
also get involved with Lady Stoneheart if

00:04:36.729 --> 00:04:38.439
she turns up.

00:04:38.439 --> 00:04:43.759
Bran Stark is beyond the Wall with Bloodraven,
aka Brynden, aka the three-eyed crow, who

00:04:43.759 --> 00:04:49.069
is giving Bran visions of the past including
this one of the fight at the Tower of Joy,

00:04:49.069 --> 00:04:54.229
between three of Aerys Targaryen’s kingsguard
and seven of Ned Stark’s men.

00:04:54.229 --> 00:04:58.719
This guy here may well be the legendary Arthur
Dayne, while the bloke who gets shishkebabed

00:04:58.719 --> 00:05:00.069
must be one of Ned’s guys.

00:05:00.069 --> 00:05:04.719
But again, the really cool thing about this
scene is that we may get to see Ned’s sister

00:05:04.719 --> 00:05:08.629
Lyanna, and the true parentage of Jon Snow.

00:05:08.629 --> 00:05:13.179
We also see Meera Reed, who apparently is
still hanging around in Bloodraven’s cave,

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:17.819
with Hodor, and Jojen, assuming he hasn’t
been eaten by Bran.

00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:23.039
And finally we see the white walkers, striding
through fire, riding four horses, with Davos

00:05:23.039 --> 00:05:25.289
describing the war to come.

00:05:25.289 --> 00:05:29.110
At this point the walkers’ve really got
two places left to strike – Bloodraven’s

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:33.300
cave, and the Wall itself.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:37.069
So that’s the second trailer – conflict
at Castle Black, huge battle in the north

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:41.449
and maybe vengeance for the Starks, tension
rising in the House of Black and White, new

00:05:41.449 --> 00:05:45.800
players in Meereen, Dany against the dosh
khaleen, Greyjoys converging on Pyke with

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:50.249
Asha sailing east, shit hitting the fan in
King’s Landing, with sparrows and Tyrells

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:54.099
and Bobby Strong fighting, and also stuff
in the riverlands, Bran on the weirwood net,

00:05:54.099 --> 00:05:59.919
Tower of Joy, Meera Jojen Hodor, and the Others,
the white walkers, on the attack.

00:05:59.919 --> 00:06:03.639
This season’s gonna be crazy, so if you’d
like to know more, check out our videos on

00:06:03.639 --> 00:06:08.529
Arya, Dany, greyscale, Euron, Robert Strong,
Jojen’s fate, Jon’s resurrection and much

00:06:08.529 --> 00:06:09.869
much more.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:13.490
Please like and subscribe, and see you next
time.

